{"book":23,"chapter":15,"context":{"chapter":15,"title":"A Lament for Moab","summary":"Isaiah grieves as Moab's cities fall in a night attack. Refugees flee south weeping, with shaved heads and sackcloth, and the land's streams run dry.","background":"Moab lay east of the Dead Sea, a kingdom descended from Lot (Genesis 19:37) and often hostile to Israel. Several towns named here, including Dibon, Medeba, Nebo, Jahaz and Horonaim, also appear on the Mesha Stele, a Moabite king's inscription from the 9th century BC found at Dhiban in 1868.","customs":[{"term":"Baldness and cut beards","verses":"15:2-3","note":"Shaving the head, cutting the beard and wearing sackcloth were mourning customs among Israel's neighbors (compare Jeremiah 48:37)."}],"watchFor":["The prophet's own grief: 'My heart shall cry out for Moab' (v. 5).","The cry spreads from town to town (vv. 2–8).","Water imagery: Nimrim dried up, Dimon full of blood (vv. 6, 9)."],"connections":["Genesis 19:37","Jeremiah 48:1-5","Jeremiah 48:37","2 Kings 3:4-5"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["מַשָּׂא","masa'","H4853","HNcmsc","[the] oracle of"],["מוֹאָב","mo'av","H4124","HNpl","Moab"],["כִּי","ki","H3588","HTc","that"],["בְּלֵיל","beleil","H3915","HR/Ncmsc","in a night"],["שֻׁדַּד","shudad","H7703","HVPp3ms","<of> [which] it was devastated"],["עָר","'ar","H6144","HNpl","Ar"],["מוֹאָב","mo'av","H4124","HNpl","of Moab"],["נִדְמָה","nidmah","H1820","HVNp3ms","it was destroyed"],["כִּי","ki","H3588","HTc","that"],["בְּלֵיל","beleil","H3915","HR/Ncmsc","in a night"],["שֻׁדַּד","shudad","H7703","HVPp3ms","<of> [which] it was devastated"],["קִיר","kir-","H7024","HNpl","Kir of"],["מוֹאָב","mo'av","H4124","HNpl","Moab"],["נִדְמָה","nidmah","H1820","HVNp3ms","it was destroyed"]],"x":[[30002001,30002003,6],[24048001,24048047,5],[4021028,4021028,4],[23011014,23011014,4],[26025008,26025011,4],[23014028,23014028,3],[23016007,23016007,3],[23016011,23016011,3],[23025010,23025010,3],[36002008,36002011,3]],"xn":11},"2":{"w":[["עָלָה","'alah"